#### Power Bi

Now, looking at the **current hiring landscape**, we can see a few key business insights.

**On the left**, we can see that around **81% of candidates have joined**, while about **19% have not joined**. This gives the business a clear view of the **joining conversion rate** and the potential gap between hiring and actual workforce availability.This also signals that our dataset is imbalanced

**On the right**, we can see the **joining volume by location**. Chennai and Noida have the highest joining volumes, followed by Bangalore and Hyderabad. This can help the business in **workforce allocation and location-wise capacity planning**.

**At the bottom left**, we can see that the average experience is **4.4 years for males and 3.5 years for females**.

And **on the bottom right**, the average CTC hike is quite similar, at around **41% for males and 40% for females**, giving us visibility into **compensation patterns**.

Overall, these insights provide a quick understanding of **joining conversion, workforce distribution, experience, and compensation**, which can support better **hiring and workforce planning decisions**
